# Helix Settings Come From wiseai.html

`pages/wiseai.html` is the single source of truth for Helix. Whatever pose
is set there — on, opacity, angle, camera, scale, knobs, look, spin, style —
is the pose every other page that has Helix must use.

The published load default lives in `BGANIM_PUBLISH_POSE` in
`js/wiseai-chat.js` (the Scene chip). Close-up stays a Load chip. A member
change on wiseai writes the shared `wise:chat-bg-anim-*` keys and every
other chat helix follows.

## Mobile view is the one sanctioned departure

Below 768px a fresh load starts from `BGANIM_PHONE_POSE` — the same Scene
pose at **35% opacity and paused**. It is app-wide (every chat module, not
one page), it lives beside the published pose rather than in a caller, and
everything reads it through `bgAnimLoadPose()`. It is a *default*: a stored
opacity or an explicit Play / Pause still wins at any width.

This is not a per-page fallback and must not be "corrected" back to Scene.

## What this means on the surface

- Open any chat with Helix → it matches the wiseai helix, not a local look.
- Fresh load (no saved preference) → Scene: on, 3D, ~50% opacity.
- Fresh load in mobile view → the same pose, dimmed to 35% and held still.
- Change a slider on wiseai → the same values land on every other helix.

## Rules for the agent

- Never invent a per-page Helix default (no `20%` / `10°` / `30%` fallbacks).
- If wiseai and another page disagree, wiseai wins — bring the other page
  into line, not the reverse.
- Read `bgAnimLoadPose()` for a load default, and `readBgAnimOpacityPct()` /
  `readBgAnimAngle()` (and the other `readBgAnim*` helpers) for live values.
  Do not hardcode pose numbers, and do not read `BGANIM_PUBLISH_POSE`
  directly where a load default is what you want — that skips mobile view.
- A new tier pose goes next to `BGANIM_PUBLISH_POSE` as a named frozen
  override of it, never as a literal inside a caller.
- Decorative still-frame helices (e.g. the paused product-photo strip on
  Add / View Product) are not the chat helix. Do not retune them to Scene.

## When in doubt

Open `pages/wiseai.html`, confirm the published Scene pose in
`js/wiseai-chat.js`, and mirror it.
